From: dinadur <59811564+dinadur@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 21:51:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/18] B70: save receipt-verified generic research to the wiki
 on explicit request

A research request that explicitly asks to save to the wiki now arms the
guarded generic research route. The controller offers only the bounded
tools, rejects stray calls and captures the receipt automatically, and
the model is told the controller will save. After the final answer
passes the receipt check, the controller (never the model) creates one
new note under research/ in OBSIDIAN_VAULT_PATH. It uses O_EXCL, never
overwrites (same-day collisions get -2, -3 ...), records the request,
the date, the receipt sources and review_status: unreviewed, rereads and
hash-checks the note, and appends "Saved to wiki: <path>" or "Not saved
to wiki: <reason>" to the reply. A negated request ("do not save ...")
does not save. User-authorized on 2026-09-27.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
